{
  "word": "获胜",
  "definition_simple": "赢得比赛或斗争",
  "definition_standard": "在竞赛、斗争或对抗中取得胜利",
  "pos": "v",
  "semantic_class": "action",
  "examples": [
    {
      "sentence": "我们获胜了。",
      "tier": "T1",
      "translation": "We won."
    },
    {
      "sentence": "这场比赛谁获胜了？",
      "tier": "T1",
      "translation": "Who won this match?"
    },
    {
      "sentence": "中国队在决赛中获胜。",
      "tier": "T2",
      "translation": "The Chinese team won the final."
    },
    {
      "sentence": "他们靠团队合作获胜。",
      "tier": "T2",
      "translation": "They won by teamwork."
    },
    {
      "sentence": "经过激烈的角逐，他终于获胜了。",
      "tier": "T3",
      "translation": "After fierce competition, he finally won."
    },
    {
      "sentence": "这场胜利使我们获得了继续前进的勇气，并在接下来的比赛中再次获胜。",
      "tier": "T4",
      "translation": "This victory gave us the courage to move forward and win again in the next match."
    },
    {
      "sentence": "想要在竞争激烈的市场中获胜，企业必须不断进行技术创新。",
      "tier": "T5",
      "translation": "To win in a highly competitive market, enterprises must continuously innovate in technology."
    },
    {
      "sentence": "辩论赛双方势均力敌，最终正方凭借严密的逻辑论证险胜获胜。",
      "tier": "T5",
      "translation": "The two sides of the debate were evenly matched, and ultimately the affirmative side narrowly won with rigorous logical arguments."
    },
    {
      "sentence": "纵观整场战役，战略上的先发制人是决定能否最终获胜的关键所在。",
      "tier": "T6",
      "translation": "Looking at the whole campaign, strategic preemption is the key to determining whether one can ultimately win."
    },
    {
      "sentence": "在博弈论的框架下，理性的参与者会寻求能够实现自身效用最大化并确保获胜的策略。",
      "tier": "T6",
      "translation": "Under the framework of game theory, rational participants will seek strategies that maximize their own utility and ensure victory."
    }
  ],
